rac{\\max_jc_j}{\\min_jc_j},\\qquad\nL24: > \\sigma=s_2\\!\\left(A\\operatorname{diag}(c)^{-1/2}\\right). \\] The input-only condition $\\sqrt K\\,\\sigma<1$ certifies exact scalability and polynomial scaling distortion, with $D=O(\\log n)$ for fixed $K$ and a fixed positive spectral margin. Given a finite scaling $B$, the weaker condition $\\sqrt K\\,\\sigma s_2(B)<1$ gives the same structural bounds. With a constant endpoint gap, these bounds imply logarithmic SK iteration complexity.\nL25: Boundary constructions show that the strict spectral inequalities cannot uniformly be replaced by nonstrict ones.\nL26: Comments:  | 71 pages\nL27: Subjects:  | Data Structures and Algorithms (cs.DS)\nL28: Cite as:  | 【8†arXiv:2611.08963】 [cs.DS]\nL29:    | (or 【9†arXiv:2611.08963v1】 [cs.DS] for this version)\nL30:    | 【10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2611.08963†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL31: ## Submission history\nL32: \nL33: From: Kun He [【11†view email】]\nL34: [v1] Fri, 6 Nov 2026 04:17:17 UTC (84 KB)\nL35: \nL36: Full-text links:\nL37: \nL38: ## Access Paper:\nL39: \nL40: View a PDF of the paper titled Global Sinkhorn Convergence and Spectral Stability of Matrix Scaling, by Kun He\nL41: \nL42:   * 【6†View PDF】\nL43:   * 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL44:   * 【12†TeX Source】\nL45: \nL46: 【13†view license】\nL47: \nL48: ### Additional Features\nL49: \nL50:   * 【14†Audio Summary】\nL51: ### Current browse context:\nL52: \nL53: cs.DS\nL54: \nL55: 【15†< prev】   |   【16†next >】\nL56: \nL57: 【17†new】 | 【18†recent】 | 【19†2026-11】\nL58: \nL59: Change to browse by:\nL60: \nL61: 【20†cs】\nL62: \nL63: ### References & Citations\nL64: \nL65:   * 【21†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL66:   * 【22†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL67:   * 【23†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL68: \nL69: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL70: \nL71: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL72: \nL73: [Button: ×]\nL74: \nL75: loading...\nL76: \nL77: Data provided by:\nL78: 