preparing the initial state.\nL17: Compared with the update bounds of the corresponding classical Gibbs sampler, our quantum walk-query complexity improves the dependence on the time horizon $T$ from quadratic to linear. For the endpoint coupling, we adapt a quantum box-constrained Newton method to compute the Schrödinger potentials, improving the matrix-scaling complexity, at fixed accuracy, from quadratic to $N^{3/2}$ in the state-space size $N$.\nL18: Finally, we show that exponential reweighting extends both the Schrödinger bridge formulation and the Gibbs spectral-gap estimate to models with additive running costs.\nL19: Comments:  | 59 pages, 1 figure\nL20: Subjects:  | Quantum Physics (quant-ph); Optimization and Control (math.OC); Probability (math.PR)\nL21: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 81P68, 60J10, 60J22, 65C40, 90C25\nL22: Cite as:  | 【8†arXiv:2609.27103】 [quant-ph]\nL23:    | (or 【9†arXiv:2609.27103v1】 [quant-ph] for this version)\nL24:    | 【10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.27103†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Eyal Neuman [【11†view email】]\nL28: [v1] Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:57:40 UTC (57 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Quantum-Enhanced Sampling of Schr\\\"odinger Bridges, by Tom Lollier and Eyal Neuman\nL35: \nL36:   * 【7†View PDF】\nL37:   * 【12†TeX Source】\nL38: \nL39: 【13†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL40: \nL41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: quant-ph\nL44: \nL45: 【14†< prev】   |   【15†next >】\nL46: \nL47: 【16†new】 | 【17†recent】 | 【18†2026-09】\nL48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: 【19†math】\nL52: 【20†math.OC】\nL53: 【21†math.PR】\nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * 【22†INSPIRE HEP†inspirehep.net】\nL57:   * 【23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL58:   * 【24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL59:   * 【25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL60: \nL61: [B